  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post-Earthquake Recovery Efforts in T&#xfc;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is&#xa0;to support local economic recovery in T&#xfc;rkiye&#xb4;s earthquakes-affected region,&#xa0;while empowering individuals with the necessary skills and competencies to foster long-term resilience. For this, IOM will assist 80 micro, small, and medium sized businesses through financial assistance grants, including pre-loaded debit cards or cash grants. IOM will coordinate closely with various government counterparts including the Disaster and Emergency Management Presidency (AFAD), Presidency of Migration Management (PMM), and Provincial Directorates of Migration Management (PDMMs) where operations are taking place, as well as municipalities and provincial-level authorities to ensure activities are aligned with national priorities. The project will run for one year from September 2023 to September 2024, with the financial support of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea.</narrative>
  </description>
